### SkatePod API sample requests
### Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (or IntelliJ) and click "Send Request".
### The IDs below come from the dev sample data.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api

### List all students (with each one's next lesson)
GET {{baseUrl}}/students

### Get one student (Emma)
GET {{baseUrl}}/students/11111111-1111-1111-1111-000000000001

### List disciplines and their levels (what the app's dropdowns show)
GET {{baseUrl}}/disciplines

### Create a student (disciplines can also be left out or empty)
POST {{baseUrl}}/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mai",
  "disciplines": [
    { "discipline": "ADULT_FREESKATE", "track": "ADULT", "level": "Adult Bronze" },
    { "discipline": "PATTERN_DANCE", "track": "ADULT", "level": "Bronze" }
  ]
}

### Validation error example (blank name, discipline without a track) → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "disciplines": [
    { "discipline": "STANDARD_FREESKATE", "level": "Bronze" }
  ]
}

### Level from another discipline → 400 (Juvenile isn't a Standard Freeskate level)
POST {{baseUrl}}/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mai",
  "disciplines": [
    { "discipline": "STANDARD_FREESKATE", "track": "CHAMPIONSHIP", "level": "Juvenile" }
  ]
}

### Update a student (the disciplines list replaces the old one)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/students/11111111-1111-1111-1111-000000000001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Emma Miller",
  "disciplines": [
    { "discipline": "STANDARD_FREESKATE", "track": "EXCEL", "level": "Gold" },
    { "discipline": "STANDARD_SKILLS", "track": "CHAMPIONSHIP", "level": "Gold" }
  ]
}

### List all weekly lessons, Monday first (each shows its place, if it's inside an availability block)
GET {{baseUrl}}/lessons

### List one student's lessons
GET {{baseUrl}}/lessons?studentId=11111111-1111-1111-1111-000000000001

### Add a weekly lesson (startDate left out = starts today; no endDate = keeps going)
POST {{baseUrl}}/lessons
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-000000000006",
  "dayOfWeek": "SUNDAY",
  "startTime": "16:30",
  "durationMinutes": 45,
  "type": "Freestyle"
}

### Double booking → 409 (send the one above first: this one starts during it, every Sunday)
POST {{baseUrl}}/lessons
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-000000000001",
  "dayOfWeek": "SUNDAY",
  "startTime": "17:00",
  "durationMinutes": 30,
  "type": "Public"
}

### A lesson for a set stretch of weeks (Sofia, Fridays in January)
POST {{baseUrl}}/lessons
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-000000000004",
  "dayOfWeek": "FRIDAY",
  "startTime": "07:00",
  "durationMinutes": 60,
  "type": "Off-ice",
  "startDate": "2027-01-01",
  "endDate": "2027-01-29"
}

### Invalid lesson type → 400 (only Public, Freestyle or Off-ice)
POST {{baseUrl}}/lessons
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-000000000004",
  "dayOfWeek": "SUNDAY",
  "startTime": "16:30",
  "durationMinutes": 45,
  "type": "Moves"
}

### Not found example → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/students/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Delete a lesson (Jonah's Friday off-ice lesson; its notes stay in the history)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/lessons/22222222-2222-2222-2222-000000000006

### Availability blocks, Monday first
GET {{baseUrl}}/availability

### Add an availability block (place is optional)
POST {{baseUrl}}/availability
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dayOfWeek": "WEDNESDAY",
  "startTime": "14:00",
  "endTime": "17:00",
  "place": "North Rink"
}

### Overlapping block → 409 (Tuesday 3–6 PM at North Rink is already there)
POST {{baseUrl}}/availability
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dayOfWeek": "TUESDAY",
  "startTime": "17:00",
  "endTime": "19:00"
}

### Training history, newest first (adds entries for lessons that started since the last check)
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes

### One student's history in a date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes?studentId=11111111-1111-1111-1111-000000000001&from=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z

### Add a past lesson (no lessonId; the date can't be in the future)
POST {{baseUrl}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-000000000003",
  "date": "2026-11-01T15:00:00Z",
  "title": "Extra session",
  "lessonType": "Public",
  "durationMinutes": 45,
  "overall": "Steady",
  "focus": "Crossovers",
  "observations": "Better knee bend on the left side.",
  "nextSteps": "Two sets each way next time.",
  "skills": ["Backward crossovers"],
  "shared": false
}

### Lily's programs (she has two: a free skate and a showcase)
GET {{baseUrl}}/programs?studentId=11111111-1111-1111-1111-000000000002

### Every student's programs
GET {{baseUrl}}/programs

### Add a program for Emma. musicFileId is optional: upload a file first (below) and paste its id.
POST {{baseUrl}}/programs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-000000000001",
  "name": "Free skate 2026-27",
  "musicTitle": "Swan Lake",
  "artist": "Tchaikovsky",
  "duration": "2:40",
  "track": "CHAMPIONSHIP",
  "level": "Juvenile",
  "musicLink": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=example",
  "elements": ["2A", "FCCoSp", "2Lz+2T", "StSq", "CCoSp"],
  "paths": [[{ "x": 40, "y": 60 }, { "x": 120, "y": 80 }]],
  "placements": [{ "id": "p1", "code": "2A", "x": 120, "y": 80 }]
}

### Level from another track → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/programs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-000000000001",
  "name": "Free skate",
  "musicTitle": "Swan Lake",
  "duration": "2:40",
  "track": "EXCEL",
  "level": "Juvenile",
  "elements": ["2A"]
}

### Upload a music file (put an MP3 called song.mp3 next to this file first). Up to 20 MB.
POST {{baseUrl}}/music
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=SkatePod

--SkatePod
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="song.mp3"
Content-Type: audio/mpeg

< ./song.mp3
--SkatePod--

### Play an uploaded file (paste the id from the upload)
GET {{baseUrl}}/music/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Tracks with their levels, and every program element
GET {{baseUrl}}/tracks

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/elements
